<div class="about-container">
    <h2>Telnyx Media Streaming Application</h2>
    <p>
        This is a comprehensive Node.js application demonstrating real-time media streaming 
        capabilities with Telnyx's Call Control API over WebSockets.
    </p>

    <h3>Features</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>📞 Outbound call initiation and management</li>
        <li>🎙️ Real-time media streaming over WebSockets</li>
        <li>☎️ DTMF digit detection and sending</li>
        <li>📊 Live call monitoring and analytics</li>
        <li>🔗 Webhook integration for call events</li>
        <li>📱 Responsive web UI with Server-Side Rendering</li>
        <li>🔐 Secure API key management</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Technology Stack</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Backend:</strong> Node.js + Express.js</li>
        <li><strong>Templating:</strong> EJS (Server-Side Rendering)</li>
        <li><strong>Styling:</strong> CSS3</li>
        <li><strong>Real-time Communication:</strong> WebSockets (ws library)</li>
        <li><strong>HTTP Client:</strong> Axios</li>
        <li><strong>API:</strong> Telnyx Call Control API v2</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>API Integration</h3>
    <p>
        This application connects to Telnyx's V2 API for call management and uses WebSockets 
        for real-time media streaming as per the Telnyx Media Streaming documentation.
    </p>

    <h3>Getting Started</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>Create a Telnyx account at https://telnyx.com</li>
        <li>Purchase a phone number</li>
        <li>Create a connection ID</li>
        <li>Copy your API key</li>
        <li>Configure the .env file</li>
        <li>Run the application</li>
        <li>Start making calls!</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Documentation</h3>
    <p>
        For more information about Telnyx Media Streaming, visit:
        <a href="https://developers.telnyx.com" target="_blank">Telnyx Developer Docs</a>
    </p>

